        "sources": [
          {
            "index": 1,
            "title": "Moonveil requirements",
            "section": "Verified fields / arithmetic constraints",
            "url": "https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Moonveil",
            "text": "Moonveil's listed one-handed requirements are Strength 12, Dexterity 18 and Intelligence 23. Requirements are distinct from scaling, recommended stats and damage; this does not establish latest-patch damage.",
            "origin": "corpus"
          },
          {
            "index": 2,
            "title": "Attribute point accounting",
            "section": "Verified fields / arithmetic constraints",
            "url": "https://eldenring.wikidot.com/stats",
            "text": "A character's level equals the sum of the eight primary attributes minus 79. Thus the target attribute sum is level + 79. Vigor affects HP; Mind affects FP; Endurance affects stamina and equip load. Arithmetic does not establish optimality.",
            "origin": "corpus"
          },
          {
            "index": 3,
            "title": "Samurai starting attributes",
            "section": "Verified fields / arithmetic constraints",
            "url": "https://wiki.eso-ui.com/index.php/Elden_Ring:Samurai",
            "text": "Samurai starts at level 9 with Vigor 12, Mind 11, Endurance 13, Strength 12, Dexterity 15, Intelligence 9, Faith 8, Arcane 8. These are starting values, not a recommended final build.",
            "origin": "corpus"
          },
          {
            "index": 4,
            "title": "Respec baseline constraints",
            "section": "Verified fields / arithmetic constraints",
            "url": "https://eip.gg/elden-ring/guides/how-to-respec/",
            "text": "Respec redistributes available attributes without lowering character level. Attributes determined by the starting class cannot be reduced below their original values. All available attribute points must be spent.",
            "origin": "corpus"
          },
          {
            "index": 5,
            "title": "Moonveil",
            "section": "Notes",
            "url": "https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Moonveil#Notes",
            "text": "The Unique Skill: Transient Moonlight is the regular Skill: Unsheathe but with added projectiles: a short-ranged one for the light attack sweep and a mid-ranged one for the heavy attack overhead slash.\nThe skill is useful in roughly the same ways that Unsheathe is, meaning that the light attack follow-up is generally slightly quicker and much wider in exchange for being slightly weaker, while the heavy attack follow-up hits a single target slightly harder and is slightly more difficult to roll directly away from.\nOne stark difference is that the different attacks are much less dissimilar, with the light attack follow-up having less of a damage difference (22% less for Unsheathe, 10% less for Transient Moonlight) and much less of a Stance damage difference (50% less for Unsheathe, 8% less for Transient Moonlight).\nWhile this does give the weapon some more reach (though mostly with the heavy attack follow-up), the skill is still the most effective at melee range since that means both the weapon and the magic waves can hit the target.\nThe skill's heavy attack follow-up has a weird interaction with jumping players and deals a lot less damage against them for some reason.\nWhile a hybrid Intelligence/Dexterity build gains the highest total Attack Power a pure Intelligence build only loses about 2% total Attack Power in exchange for the skill's projectiles getting 13% higher Attack Power, making the latter generally preferable.",
            "origin": "corpus"
          }
        ],
        "images": [
          {
            "id": "7a71153edfa4ea6c2e4b6a6fc13249306bea1c479ac7cdff0c18eceb9a204b23",
            "url": "/api/v1/images/7a71153edfa4ea6c2e4b6a6fc13249306bea1c479ac7cdff0c18eceb9a204b23",
            "caption": null,
            "alt": "Notes",
            "source_url": "https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Moonveil#Notes",
            "source_indices": [
              5
            ],
            "attribution": null,
            "license": null,
            "license_status": "unknown_review_required",
            "file_page_url": "https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/File:ER_Main_Menu_Icon_Messages.png",
            "game_scope": "elden_ring",
            "release_scope": "base_candidate"
          }
        ],
        "clarification": null,
        "answer": "Moonveil cần Strength 12, Dexterity 18 và Intelligence 23 để dùng một tay [1]. Với Samurai (bắt đầu level 9: Vigor 12, Mind 11, Endurance 13, Strength 12, Dexterity 15, Intelligence 9, Faith 8, Arcane 8) [3], lên level 100 nghĩa là tổng tám chỉ số phải bằng 179 [2], và vì respec không thể hạ chỉ số dưới mức gốc của class, mọi phân bổ đều phải tôn trọng các mức sàn đó [4].\n\nMột ví dụ khả thi cho PvE thuần Moonveil (đây là gợi ý, không phải tối ưu đã kiểm chứng): ưu tiên Intelligence và Dexterity vì Moonveil là vũ khí lai Int/Dex, dồn phần còn lại cho Vigor/Mind/Endurance để sống sót và đủ FP dùng skill. Chỉ số cụ thể ở khối phân bổ bên dưới; bạn có thể chỉnh lại tùy theo việc bạn spam Transient Moonlight nhiều hay đánh cận chiến nhiều hơn [5].\n\nVí dụ phân bổ hợp lệ về điểm/requirements, chưa xác minh tối ưu:\nVigor 43 | Mind 18 | Endurance 20 | Strength 12 | Dexterity 24 | Intelligence 46 | Faith 8 | Arcane 8 [1][2][3][4]\n\nĐây là một ví dụ hợp lệ về mặt số học và yêu cầu vũ khí, không phải build tối ưu; mình chưa thể xác nhận các mốc soft cap hay hiệu suất theo patch hiện tại."
      },
